Z||000000||MooCow||01-19-2000||08:10 AM||||I'm a 17 year old and I will have around $5,000 to spend on a Fiero in April of this year.  What kind of Fiero in what shape could I get.  I really want an auto V6 with air,cruise,tilt,power windows and locks, & a sunroof with around 70,000 miles or so.  Am I dreaming or would I be able to find this car for that price here in Muskegon Michigan??||||reg||5
Z||000001||DJRice||01-19-2000||08:43 AM||||If you have that kind of $ to spend, I think you'll be able to find something real nice.<P>Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||01-19-2000||08:51 AM||||For $5000, you should be able to find an 85-87 GT, 85-87 SE, or 88 Formula with fewer than 75,000 miles with beautiful paint and clean interior that has never been wrecked and runs like new.  For $5000, a notchback V6 should even smell new.<P>Your budget won't go quite as far with the 88 GT's (you might have to settle for a few more miles), but you should still be able to find a beauty.<P>Incidentally, if I were you, I wouldn't limit your search to your home state.  Wouldn't it be worth a trip to, say, Georgia or Arizona to have a more rust-free car?  My 88 Coupe is an OH car - its frame is rust free, but some of the suspension components are showing surface rust.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||TwisT||01-19-2000||10:08 AM||||Just as a note...  I spent a whopping total of $4400 on my absolutely mint condition '88 GT with 47,000 miles on it.  In fact,  I bought it with Ocelot exhaust,  the cat removed,  Hypertech chip,  low-temp fan sensor,  new clutch,  K&N filter,  new tires,  aftermarket stereo,  etc...  even had a complete A-to-Z log of all service work done on it since new!  Synthetic oil even...<P>And guess where I found this gem?  On the Internet!  The downside?  I had to drive to Moline Illinois to get it.  Worth it?  You bet your Fiero-butt!!!<P>TIP:  Watch those "for sale" sections on websites.  You'd be surprised (as was I) as to what kind of deals you can find!<P>Coincidently,  I also found another '88 GT with many mods for sale at the same time...  it was blue,  had a few more miles  (74,000), not quite as nice...  but for $3800!  <P>Happy Fiero-ing!    ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave85||01-19-2000||12:35 PM||||I just ran across this. It was posted about a month ago but you never know.<P>88 GT with 75,000 miles, black,loaded,new exhaust. $4950!!  The phone# is 607.770.9100 (NY)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Dave85 (edited 01-19-2000).]||||reg||1
